  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/... \nEnsembles continue to point towards the subtropical high shifting\nback eastwards starting Friday as a troughing feature moves\ninto the Northwestern U.S./ Canadian boarder. As the trough \npushes eastwards PWATs begin to improve, being back above normal, \nnear 1.5\"-1.7\" by Saturday, and is expected to remain through at \nleast the weekend. 1000-700MB mixing ratios are forecasted to be \ngenerally back above 10 g/kg which should be enough for rain \nchances to return to the region as the NBM/WPC PoPs are currently \nreflecting a 20-30% chance. This is a decent increase from \nprevious runs but still several days out so models are still \nsubject to change, but currently looks promising for at least the \neastern high terrain. Temperatures will notably reduce by Sunday \nfor most of the region, falling to near normal.",
